From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 05:49:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/24] node-executor: retire unhealthy local generations

Use one absolute deadline across local Node request submission, response headers, and response streaming. Retire the selected generation on timeout, transport failure, child exit, repeated watchdog failure, or backend shutdown, and lazily start one replacement for the next request.

Fence retirement by generation identity and serialize startup outside generation-state locking. Transfer the direct child and tempdir to cancellation-safe cleanup, delete the tempdir only after confirmed reaping, and preserve it when runtime teardown or a wait failure leaves reaping unconfirmed.

Bound startup probes and invocation responses, isolate child stdio from backend logs, and keep diagnostics fixed and sanitized. Parse streamed NDJSON with bounded bytes and parts, reject duplicate results immediately, and retire the generation for every post-header reqwest transport failure.

Record bounded attribution for the initiating request kind, phase, sanitized transport category, child state before termination, supervisor signal ownership, final exit class, and replacement outcome. Keep generation IDs in structured logs rather than metric labels, and never retain raw requests, transport errors, stdout, or stderr.

Track cancellation-safe waiting and active requests and export bounded generation, child, request, watchdog, replacement, package, stack, and retirement-diagnostic metrics. Keep the executor single-process and document the direct-child ownership and rollback contract.
